// The other half of the same rule (see const_expression_range_checked_narrow.saw):
// a constant EXPRESSION reaching a repeat literal's VALUE adopts the declared
// element width, so it is range-checked there too. `1 << 20` does not fit
// `UInt16`, and `[1 << 20; 2]` at `[UInt16; 2]` is now the same clean error.
//
// This is the position family that did not truncate but WIDENED: the value and
// its backing storage used to be carried at platform width while the declared
// Saw type claimed `UInt16`, so the array printed the untruncated `1048576`
// (DF-235b). Its siblings — an Optional payload slot (`let o: UInt16? =
// 1 << 20`), the `??` operand (`absent ?? (1 << 20)`), and a UNIFORM plain
// array literal whose elements are all const expressions — reach the same
// funnel case and are covered by it rather than re-pinned.
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: does not fit in `UInt16`

func main() {
    let r: [UInt16; 2] = [1 << 20; 2]
    print("{r[0]}")
}
